  "body": "Document has associated URL (https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-url), which is some URL from URL spec. But this internal state is directly represented as DOMString or is a more complex structure? I ask because Document.documentURI and Document.URL attributes must return the URL, without any serialization, what is oposite to \"6.6. URL APIs elsewhere\" (https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#url-apis-elsewhere).  In the other site URL spec has concept like URL string (https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url).\n",
